From: RitzDaCat <49771174+RitzDaCat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:10:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] core: add refresh-relative adaptive timing budgets

Feed the unclamped render span to the controller while the stock journal
keeps its 2 ms floor for fail-closed operation. Learn a bounded render budget independently
for each presentation path from the second-largest duration in a fixed sample
window. Live mode uses a refresh-derived first-frame bootstrap, adopts the first
raw render span, gives one-off overruns a short emergency reserve, raises the
persistent budget on repeated tails, and decays after clean windows.

Replace the older fixed-time wake-margin floor, guard, decay, and hard ceiling
with bounds derived from each output's refresh duration. Both live controllers
operate in nanoseconds, isolate state by output and presentation path, and
contain no fixed millisecond tuning constants.
